WEBVTT

01:22.120 --> 01:25.480
Pine decorations, sacred shrine rope, your written New Year's resolution, a Daruma doll,

01:22.120 --> 01:29.690
[Note: Daruma doll is a traditional Japanese doll that's regarded as a talisman of good luck.]

01:25.480 --> 01:29.690
and the other items used during New Year's; did everyone bring them?

01:29.690 --> 01:31.070
Yup!

01:32.650 --> 01:36.110
Before starting your burning, please remove all plastic items.

01:36.110 --> 01:39.280
Okay, I'm lighting it.

01:47.710 --> 01:49.290
[Note: The paper says "Will Power"]

01:58.090 --> 02:05.560
Houshou
Wanya

01:58.830 --> 02:02.520
I heard that if you roast the leftover New Year's mochi

01:58.830 --> 02:02.520
[Note: Mochi are Japanese rice cakes made from glutinous rice.]

02:02.520 --> 02:05.560
using this fire and eat them, you won't catch any colds.

02:06.040 --> 02:09.050
Though, of course, mine are dangos.

02:09.050 --> 02:12.310
I even made them myself.

02:12.310 --> 02:15.490
Red ones, white ones... so auspicious.

02:15.490 --> 02:19.290
In a lot of different shapes too... so much fun.

02:19.290 --> 02:24.560
I'll roast them and put a tangy sweet sauce on them... I can't wait!

02:27.500 --> 02:32.460
Matching Kimonos with Miyu

02:35.110 --> 02:36.200
Here we go!

02:36.200 --> 02:37.150
Fireworks?

02:37.150 --> 02:38.800
Aren't those the ones you bought in the summer?

02:38.800 --> 02:40.830
Wouldn't they be damp by now?

02:40.830 --> 02:44.020
Nope. They're fine.

02:44.020 --> 02:46.590
I packed them with a desiccant, wrapped them in newspaper,

02:46.590 --> 02:49.740
placed them in a can, and stored them in a cool place.

02:49.740 --> 02:53.560
If you do all that, the fireworks produced will be even prettier than before.

02:53.860 --> 02:55.560
I've never heard that before.

02:55.560 --> 02:59.340
So it's something like leaving stew overnight to make it tastier,

02:59.340 --> 03:01.730
but does that really apply to fireworks too?

03:02.780 --> 03:06.910
A picture is worth a thousand words. Stop complaining and just try it!

03:07.350 --> 03:09.200
Well, I guess it's true.

03:10.800 --> 03:12.670
How pretty...

03:14.380 --> 03:16.370
They all lit.

03:16.370 --> 03:19.840
Though it sounded extremely suspicious when Kurosu-ku said it,

03:19.840 --> 03:23.310
I guess as a method for preserving fireworks it's true, right?

03:23.310 --> 03:26.890
Though it sounded extremely suspicious when Kurosu-kun said it.

03:26.890 --> 03:28.350
Leave me alone!

03:28.830 --> 03:31.190
I'm going to set one off, so make sure you're watching!

03:43.800 --> 03:45.680
Amazing! Amazing!

03:45.680 --> 03:46.870
I want to see more fireworks!

03:46.870 --> 03:48.590
Hey, Saionji-kun!

03:48.590 --> 03:50.070
Can you light another one?

03:50.070 --> 03:53.440
Shouldn't you be asking me that? I'm the one who lit that firework.

03:53.920 --> 03:56.380
[Note: Text reads "When lighting fireworks, please ensure you have a bucket of water prepared."]

03:57.190 --> 03:58.420
Miyu-chan,

03:59.000 --> 04:02.880
that's a really lovely kimono.

04:06.460 --> 04:08.180
Y-You think so?

04:08.870 --> 04:10.380
Does it suit me?

04:11.580 --> 04:13.230
Yup. Yup.

04:15.360 --> 04:16.970
This kimono's...

04:20.740 --> 04:22.000
It's not here! Not here! Not here!

04:22.000 --> 04:22.940
It's not here!

04:22.940 --> 04:26.070
I thought I brought it with me, but it's not here!

04:27.300 --> 04:28.660
That's so weird...

04:28.660 --> 04:30.760
I wonder where it is...

04:30.760 --> 04:33.250
Everyone's going to be wearing kimonos.

04:33.250 --> 04:36.540
I'm sure I brought my kimono...

04:36.540 --> 04:38.590
I wonder why I can't find it...

04:39.520 --> 04:43.340
All right! I'm going to hunt for it one more time.

04:45.330 --> 04:47.610
Did I leave it at my house after all?

04:50.120 --> 04:51.630
Wear that.

04:57.300 --> 04:58.980
This kimono...

04:58.980 --> 05:00.350
Miyu-chan.

05:00.350 --> 05:01.440
Hey, Miyu-chan.

05:02.590 --> 05:04.480
Is something wrong?

05:04.480 --> 05:06.410
I-It's nothing.

05:12.830 --> 05:14.590
It's so pretty!

05:16.250 --> 05:20.870
Momoka-chan, we have lots of small fireworks here, so come and play.

05:20.870 --> 05:23.230
Really?! Ruu-kun.

05:36.710 --> 05:38.650
Hey, Ruu, aren't they...

05:38.650 --> 05:40.400
Ruu?

05:43.310 --> 05:44.540
What's that?

05:44.540 --> 05:45.880
A firework?

05:47.380 --> 05:50.030
What? You want that one lighted too?

05:50.030 --> 05:56.420
Yes, but it's dangerous for us kids to do it, so please will you light it for us, Santa oji-chan?

05:56.420 --> 05:58.020
Sure, I will.

05:58.020 --> 06:00.370
Hey, everyone, watch this!

06:00.370 --> 06:05.810
The final big firework of the night will be set off by I, Kurosu Santa, right now!

06:05.810 --> 06:07.360
Kurosu-kun, stop dragging it out.

06:07.360 --> 06:09.430
Okay! Let's go!

06:16.720 --> 06:18.850
Amazing!

06:25.570 --> 06:27.110
What's this?

06:27.110 --> 06:28.740
Isn't this kind of strange?

06:29.060 --> 06:31.460
Either way, let's go inside, everyone.

06:42.900 --> 06:43.880
What's wrong, Miyu?

06:43.880 --> 06:44.980
Let's go inside.

06:52.840 --> 06:54.340
What?

07:01.270 --> 07:03.910
I wonder what happened with that last firework...

07:03.910 --> 07:06.760
I'm sure it was just supposed to be like that.

07:06.760 --> 07:09.180
Lately, the ones they sell are really exciting.

07:09.180 --> 07:11.230
I guess so.

07:11.230 --> 07:14.620
Shall I pour some tea? I'm sure everyone's thirsty by now.

07:14.620 --> 07:16.410
I'd like to use your restroom please.

07:23.860 --> 07:26.050
Why is this in here?

07:29.240 --> 07:32.420
Why is the fuel tank open?

07:34.080 --> 07:37.190
The UFO's fuel rod's gone!

07:43.300 --> 07:46.430
Restrooms of old houses sure are located far away.

07:46.430 --> 07:50.610
Though my house is big, so the bathroom's far there too.

07:50.900 --> 07:52.150
This must be it.

08:05.340 --> 08:07.590
O-Okame-chan!

08:18.990 --> 08:20.880
They both sure are taking their time...

08:20.880 --> 08:24.030
Hey, uncle isn't in the kitchen.

08:28.480 --> 08:33.150
Everyone, run away as fast as you can!

09:04.520 --> 09:06.340
What on earth was that?

09:06.340 --> 09:08.130
Why a dinosaur?

09:09.150 --> 09:12.440
Hey, isn't it weirdly quiet?

09:13.460 --> 09:15.550
Ruu-kun and Wanya have disappeared!

09:16.060 --> 09:20.350
I'm not sure what's going on, but we've got to save everyone-

09:24.060 --> 09:25.000
Kanata!

09:59.100 --> 10:00.340
This is...

10:05.340 --> 10:08.510
Could this be a... distortion in time and space?

10:08.510 --> 10:11.340
What should I do? Kanata!

10:13.830 --> 10:15.000
Okame-chan?

10:15.000 --> 10:17.260
I'm still being chased!

10:17.610 --> 10:18.960
Nozomu-kun!

10:41.750 --> 10:48.040
The Western town magistrate, Nishiyama Saemon, has arrived.

10:50.840 --> 10:53.350
Now, homeless man, Santa, according to the accusations,

10:53.350 --> 10:58.340
you sneaked into the Nagato store and tried to steal gold and so forth.

10:58.340 --> 10:59.970
Is this true?

10:59.970 --> 11:02.950
Of course not! How did it turn out like this?

11:02.950 --> 11:05.750
I would never do anything like that.

11:05.750 --> 11:06.890
That's so mean!

11:07.210 --> 11:11.400
For what other reason would you be here then?

11:11.400 --> 11:16.130
I don't know. Isn't this a movie set?

11:16.130 --> 11:20.360
After been forced to sit here out of the blue, I don't even know what's going on anymore!

11:20.360 --> 11:22.550
Quiet! Quiet!

11:22.550 --> 11:25.330
Your strange form of speech and your suspicious clothing,

11:25.330 --> 11:31.580
you may deceive the sun, but you cannot deceive I, who has this Fubuku manju tattoo!

11:25.330 --> 11:31.580
[Note: This is a pun on Toyama no Kin-san, a popular TV character based on the life of Toyama Kagemoto.]

11:36.090 --> 11:41.910
Even if you say that, I haven't done anything bad.

11:41.910 --> 11:43.510
Please understand!

11:48.580 --> 11:49.780
What should we do?

11:49.780 --> 11:53.390
I'd like to help him, but there's really nothing we can do.

11:53.390 --> 11:58.450
How about we both jump in and take him back during the confusion?

11:58.450 --> 12:00.490
Do you really think we can do something like that?

12:00.490 --> 12:01.340
It's impossible.

12:01.340 --> 12:02.560
It's impossible.

12:02.560 --> 12:07.770
Now that I think about it, I'm sure Kurosu-kun once mentioned that he'd like to live in the Edo era.

12:07.770 --> 12:09.120
Did he?

12:09.120 --> 12:11.710
Move!

12:25.970 --> 12:28.790
Wah! Tyrannosaurus!

12:28.790 --> 12:30.680
Wh-What are you?!

12:31.140 --> 12:33.720
Your strange form of speech and your suspicious clothing,

12:33.720 --> 12:37.690
you may deceive the sun, but you cannot deceive I, who has this Fubuku manju-

12:37.690 --> 12:39.850
Oh my!

12:49.520 --> 12:52.930
After dinosaurs, we get policemen now?!

12:52.930 --> 12:55.270
They're pretty persistent.

12:55.270 --> 12:58.600
Well, we're super suspicious after all.

12:58.600 --> 13:00.250
We can't talk ourselves out of this mess!

13:02.410 --> 13:05.430
There's a moat in front of us!

13:16.370 --> 13:18.170
Oh, it's everyone else.

13:18.170 --> 13:19.190
Miyu-chan.

13:19.560 --> 13:21.370
I'm glad we all found each other.

13:21.370 --> 13:23.610
I was wondering what would happen.

13:23.920 --> 13:25.140
Where's Chris-chan?

13:25.140 --> 13:26.700
That's right! It's terrible!

13:26.700 --> 13:29.370
Chris-chan's about to be forced to marry!

13:29.370 --> 13:31.080
What?!

13:32.400 --> 13:37.290
See, that weird mustache man really likes her.

13:38.290 --> 13:39.250
That's really amazing.

13:39.610 --> 13:44.130
But Chris-chan seems to think it's some sort of play or something.

13:44.130 --> 13:48.320
If it continues on like this, he might force her to marry him.

13:48.320 --> 13:49.260
That's terrible.

13:49.260 --> 13:53.280
That's bad. If something like that happens, history would change.

13:53.280 --> 13:59.340
Well, after a dinosaur appeared in the Edo era, it kind of doesn't really matter any more, right?

13:59.340 --> 14:04.210
But Saionji-kun, Ruu-kun, and the others are still missing.

14:04.210 --> 14:05.920
We don't have time for this.

14:05.920 --> 14:07.200
What should we do?

14:11.660 --> 14:14.370
Oh! Everyone's here.

14:14.370 --> 14:18.650
Look at this dress. I really want Kanata-kun to see me in it.

14:18.650 --> 14:22.140
There's no time to be saying such carefree things!

14:23.340 --> 14:25.070
My, where's Kanata-kun?

14:25.070 --> 14:29.450
Saionji-kun and the others are still missing, and we're in big trouble too!

14:29.450 --> 14:33.760
Oh no! Kanata-kun's missing?!

14:34.090 --> 14:36.290
Exactly, what's-

14:52.310 --> 14:53.120
What?

14:57.940 --> 15:00.140
We're back at Saionji.

15:01.880 --> 15:04.790
Isn't this wonderful, Okame-chan?!

15:04.790 --> 15:07.410
Where's Kanata-kun?

15:07.410 --> 15:11.140
Why did it turn out like this?!

15:12.370 --> 15:14.990
I wonder if it's because of some monster again.

15:14.990 --> 15:16.600
Ruu-kun's gone too.

15:19.960 --> 15:25.690
In that case, let's just open up all of the other sliding doors.

15:26.180 --> 15:29.240
Before that, can you untie me first?

15:41.540 --> 15:42.580
Wow!

15:45.820 --> 15:48.790
This world's perfect for me.

15:48.790 --> 15:50.360
Chris-chan, no!

15:53.800 --> 15:56.190
Wow!

15:56.190 --> 15:58.790
Wrong place.

16:12.960 --> 16:16.270
Why are there so many different worlds?

16:16.270 --> 16:18.810
Saionji-kun! Where are you?

16:20.040 --> 16:22.290
All that's left is the main temple.

16:44.390 --> 16:46.020
Ruu-kun!

16:46.950 --> 16:48.860
Oh! Everyone came.

16:48.860 --> 16:51.160
I'm glad we found you both.

16:54.000 --> 16:58.050
It's all because Ruu-chama mistook the fuel rod for the UFO with fireworks

16:58.050 --> 17:01.160
that time-space has become warped and I turned out like this.

17:01.470 --> 17:04.260
Everything's okay now. Let's go home.

17:08.340 --> 17:12.800
Wah! Save me too!

17:17.090 --> 17:18.240
Ruu-kun!

17:40.040 --> 17:41.420
What just happened?

17:41.420 --> 17:42.750
I don't know.

17:42.750 --> 17:44.710
Ruu-kun's flying.

17:44.710 --> 17:47.960
What a strange reality-defying world, right?

17:48.450 --> 17:56.280
Ruu-kun, thank you, but please don't fly or use your powers in front of everyone, okay?

17:56.700 --> 17:57.740
Papa.

17:57.740 --> 18:00.680
That's right. We need to hurry and find Kanata.

18:00.680 --> 18:04.300
Before that, please save me!

18:04.300 --> 18:08.400
Everyone, haven't you forgotten about me?!

18:15.340 --> 18:16.900
Miyu-chi!

18:19.910 --> 18:21.470
Miyu-chi!

18:35.020 --> 18:35.990
Huh?

18:38.240 --> 18:41.270
Wh-Where is this?

18:43.080 --> 18:45.290
This gate's...

18:46.240 --> 18:48.000
Are you here visiting?

18:57.550 --> 18:58.360
Oh!

18:59.610 --> 19:00.570
It's the same...

19:00.570 --> 19:01.970
What a coincidence.

19:01.970 --> 19:03.540
It's the same pattern.

19:11.710 --> 19:13.240
This boy...

19:13.240 --> 19:15.010
I'm sorry.

19:15.880 --> 19:19.060
He really likes this pattern.

19:19.060 --> 19:21.460
He seems surprised because it's the same pattern.

19:23.830 --> 19:25.600
What are you doing, Kanata!

19:37.320 --> 19:39.760
Kanata's mother?

19:59.510 --> 20:02.950
Kanata! That's in the opposite direction of your mother.

20:05.150 --> 20:06.730
Oh, I'm sorry.

20:07.350 --> 20:09.620
But don't you...

20:09.620 --> 20:11.060
It's not like...

20:11.460 --> 20:13.580
anything would change.

20:14.800 --> 20:19.570
I guess so. But if you don't go now, you'll never get to see your mother again.

20:19.570 --> 20:20.690
You're too persistent.

20:21.000 --> 20:23.200
It's fine.

20:25.470 --> 20:27.590
What?! Don't cry!

20:27.590 --> 20:29.420
I was too harsh.

20:29.420 --> 20:31.150
I'm okay. I'm okay.

20:32.950 --> 20:36.290
I know that nothing would change,

20:36.870 --> 20:37.900
but even so,

20:37.900 --> 20:42.010
I thought your mother would like to see what you will look like after you've grown up.

21:31.060 --> 21:34.880
Oh! Miyu-chan and Saionji-kun came back!

21:34.880 --> 21:36.380
You came back together!

21:36.900 --> 21:41.550
Kanata-kun! I'm so glad you're safe! I was so worried!

21:41.550 --> 21:43.100
You came back!

21:43.100 --> 21:44.980
Now everyone's back together again, right?

21:44.980 --> 21:47.630
So exactly what happened?

21:47.630 --> 21:49.370
I don't really understand.

21:49.370 --> 21:51.710
But it was fun, so it's okay.

21:51.710 --> 21:54.550
Kanata's house really is paradise, right?

21:54.550 --> 21:55.750
Yup!

22:11.860 --> 22:14.020
Thank you for having us!

22:29.550 --> 22:30.940
I'm glad.

22:38.120 --> 22:40.850
Kanata, thank you for lending me this kimono.

22:41.950 --> 22:42.960
Miyu,

22:44.840 --> 22:47.840
that kimono looks pretty good on you.

22:50.930 --> 22:52.930
Wanya's diary.

22:52.930 --> 22:56.520
I'm glad that everyone was able to return to their own eras,

22:56.810 --> 23:00.990
but I wonder why Ruu-chama didn't save me?

23:00.990 --> 23:04.440
I'm sure he would have saved me later.

23:04.440 --> 23:10.800
Even more than that, I regret not being able to eat my dango.

24:29.990 --> 24:59.960
Next Episode

24:31.530 --> 24:34.840
That mail-order planet that Wanya's always buying things from is really convenient.

24:34.840 --> 24:37.290
But sometimes really weird stuff comes in.

24:37.290 --> 24:39.380
You need to be careful of things you don't know.

24:39.380 --> 24:40.970
I wonder what this is?

24:40.970 --> 24:43.460
Oh! Is this a cookie? It looks good! Thanks!

24:43.460 --> 24:46.490
Next time on Daa Daa Daa: Miyu and child Kanata.

24:46.490 --> 24:48.290
Huh? Kanata, where did you go?

24:48.290 --> 24:49.460
Who's this little boy?

24:49.460 --> 24:51.680
Num, num, yummy, yummy, num num...

24:51.680 --> 24:53.430
Kanata-san's turned into a child!

24:54.010 --> 24:59.960
Miyu and child Kanata

24:54.740 --> 24:56.530
Oh no!
